{
 "profile_id": "endumeni",
 "profile_name": "Endumeni Local Municipality (Dundee)",
 "short_name": "Endumeni",
 "_doc": "Emunsoft statement in two variants: 8 bills as the standard layout (METER READINGS with reading date + type), 2 newer bills with CONSUMPTION / LEVIED AMOUNT / READING DATES (start date glued in front of the meter number, end date at the line end). Fingerprint: Endumeni's own VAT number + 'ENDUMENI LOCAL MUNICIPALITY'. Electricity lines: ELECTRICITY (kWh, energy -> standard), KVA DEMAND (-> demand), BASIC ELECTRICITY (-> other); one bill also carries council seasonal-tariff reversals and re-bills (REVERSAL OF SEASONAL TARIFF, DN ELECTRICITY, DN KVA DEMAND, ADJUSTED ... BILLING) which are electricity and go to other_r (its total ex VAT is therefore low). Reading rows of type N (zero, not read) are skipped. IDENTITY x_elec_resid_r = TOTAL DUE - Opening Balance - every non-electricity ledger line (payments, other services, interest, rebates) - the VAT line, i.e. the electricity total implied by the bill's own balance movement, independent of the electricity lines; 0.00 gap on all 10 bills (10 checked). The levied-layout's LEVIED AMOUNT for the kWh row also equals the energy line.",
 "fingerprint": {
  "all": [
   "4410193041",
   "ENDUMENI LOCAL MUNICIPALITY"
  ]
 },
 "sections": {
  "electricity": {
   "start": "^[ \\t]*METER READINGS",
   "require": "^[ \\t]*\\d{2}/\\d{2}/\\d{4}[ \\t]+\\S+[ \\t]+(?:BASIC ELECTRICI|KVA DEMAND|ELECTRICITY)"
  }
 },
